                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "189b4eef-bc5d-4d70-a283-0c1b70493238",
                        "source_entry_id": "92570938-f05c-3d43-b565-cce71ebbd163",
                        "source_sense_id": "0777d791-62b9-395f-beab-f90bc14f2cdc",
                        "source_sense_description": "soort raadsel",
                        "target_lang_word": "Rebus",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Rebus",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5e731735-494f-3c1e-b1c3-672b3bdf41f6",
                                        "entry_id": "2c8f46e8-aab8-3980-b34f-a9c6a0cbd8d9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Rätsel aus aneinandergereihten Bildchen von Gegenständen mit einzelnen (zum Teil durchgestrichenen) Buchstaben, manchmal auch Ziffern, dazwischen; daraus soll ein Wort erraten werden, das mit den dargestellten Dingen inhaltlich nichts zu tun hat"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a8bfe3c0-8d90-4d14-9a96-a8580372edf4",
                                                "sense_id": "5e731735-494f-3c1e-b1c3-672b3bdf41f6",
                                                "text": "Das ist ein Rebus."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8326dda3-5153-4643-a051-bf90713679b0",
                                                "sense_id": "5e731735-494f-3c1e-b1c3-672b3bdf41f6",
                                                "text": "„Bei solch einem Rebus könnte etwa das Bild einer Mohnpflanze gefolgt von dem Buchstaben (Phonogramm) D das Wort Mond ergeben.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4f544b9e-2f42-4d4a-8c04-204c9319e5c0",
                                                "sense_id": "5e731735-494f-3c1e-b1c3-672b3bdf41f6",
                                                "text": "„Diese Wortlautschrift erlaubt es nun auch, nach dem Prinzip des Bilderrätsels, des Rebus (…) aus ursprünglichen Bildzeichen neue Abstraktbegriffe zusammenzusetzen;…“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "451840a6-e411-4513-a403-0d9037b36d34",
                                                "sense_id": "5e731735-494f-3c1e-b1c3-672b3bdf41f6",
                                                "text": "„Dies wird besonders im Fall der chinesischen Schrift mit ihrer langen, kontinuierlichen Tradition offensichtlich, wo die ursprüngliche Exklusivität der Logographie in späteren Entwicklungsphasen durch die Ergänzung des Rebus durchbrochen wurde.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cc260ba2-5c7a-4c6e-9fa5-170e6139204b",
                        "source_entry_id": "92570938-f05c-3d43-b565-cce71ebbd163",
                        "source_sense_id": "0777d791-62b9-395f-beab-f90bc14f2cdc",
                        "source_sense_description": "soort raadsel",
                        "target_lang_word": "Bilderrätsel",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Bilderrätsel",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c2e32480-9d98-313f-a578-887f72d2a3e9",
                                        "entry_id": "c1083895-aa7e-3515-8e17-f50ae9f8cfd7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Aufgabe, eine Lösung (zum Beispiel das Lösungswort, ein Sprichwort oder einen Satz) durch Raten und Nachdenken herauszubekommen, indem man Bilder und die Bedeutungen von Einzelheiten kombiniert, die im Bild vorkommen"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "661f7824-adfd-4a5e-b98e-221d809e512f",
                                                "sense_id": "c2e32480-9d98-313f-a578-887f72d2a3e9",
                                                "text": "Der Gast hatte das Bilderrätsel schnell richtig erraten, deshalb wurde er auch eingeladen, am Abendempfang teilzunehmen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e768162f-2566-4d1f-ab49-3e10185d7916",
                                                "sense_id": "c2e32480-9d98-313f-a578-887f72d2a3e9",
                                                "text": "Die WDR-Sendung »Zimmer Frei« war für die Spiele, die Gespräche auf Augenhöhe und für ihre Bilderrätsel bekannt."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ea6ab608-2bf4-4f9b-b5bb-e9734320d09d",
                        "source_entry_id": "92570938-f05c-3d43-b565-cce71ebbd163",
                        "source_sense_id": "0777d791-62b9-395f-beab-f90bc14f2cdc",
                        "source_sense_description": "soort raadsel",
                        "target_lang_word": "rebus",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "rebus",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3e8efb16-f625-3276-8842-137368c9103b",
                                        "entry_id": "22aca788-2f21-376b-9562-4375b88b3045",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An arrangement of pictures, symbols, and/or words representing phrases or words, especially as a word puzzle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "05895b6e-7837-47e5-8c1d-7729d480bd7e",
                                                "sense_id": "3e8efb16-f625-3276-8842-137368c9103b",
                                                "text": "I back him at a Rebus or a Charade against the best Rhymer in the Kingdom—has your Ladyship heard the Epigram he wrote last week on Lady Frizzle's Feather catching Fire—"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "011aec77-afd8-3a38-ae42-ce59afb8f3b9",
                                        "entry_id": "22aca788-2f21-376b-9562-4375b88b3045",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A pictographic component of a compound character (e.g. sinograph) used to hint at the pronunciation of the compound."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aaf78990-23f3-343e-a99c-87cd5268fddd",
                                        "entry_id": "22aca788-2f21-376b-9562-4375b88b3045",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An arrangement of pictures on a coat of arms which suggests the name of the person to whom it belongs."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "specifically"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a7f1c49a-4a08-4f21-af28-92b0f4802643",
                                                "sense_id": "aaf78990-23f3-343e-a99c-87cd5268fddd",
                                                "text": "The prior [Will Bolton] used to come out here to hunt in summer and recreate himself, and his rebus—a barrel or tun shot through with a crossbow bolt—is set into the garden walls."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fbd407bf-fcd1-3a34-8b8f-e1a696cdfeaf",
                                        "entry_id": "22aca788-2f21-376b-9562-4375b88b3045",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A type of crossword puzzle in which some squares contain entire words, or symbols representing words, instead of single letters."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "92b3e0c7-90d7-4a04-bab8-aa2038af5b2a",
                                                "sense_id": "fbd407bf-fcd1-3a34-8b8f-e1a696cdfeaf",
                                                "text": "Instead of spelling out card suits, for example, perhaps the constructor inserted a \"rebus,\" or picture icon for clubs, hearts, spades, or diamonds in one answer box."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "53916cf7-8bb7-45ea-8516-826762636bc6",
                                                "sense_id": "fbd407bf-fcd1-3a34-8b8f-e1a696cdfeaf",
                                                "text": "Rebuses are a vital part of cryptic crosswords and even themed standard crossword puzzles, as modernized under the leadership of Will Shortz at The New York Times, make use of rebuses."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff3bc711-9c7b-4cf8-9915-4ddf7c5b7d83",
                                                "sense_id": "fbd407bf-fcd1-3a34-8b8f-e1a696cdfeaf",
                                                "text": "In the cruciverse, a rebus refers to a crossword that violates the basic \"one letter per box\" rule, requiring the entry of multiple letters - or even a number or symbol - into a single square"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "rebus",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6c9eb0c5-a1a9-3cf9-81bf-116f76056a91",
                                        "entry_id": "0b06e31c-0067-3356-9a60-b04588d337cf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To represent (a phrase or word) as a rebus."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "rare",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8d8bd83a-fcf9-36b1-a627-02562b7154a6",
                                        "entry_id": "0b06e31c-0067-3356-9a60-b04588d337cf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To apply a rebus to (something)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "rare",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a5f956d-b53a-4d21-a85f-8dc1395ed887",
                                                "sense_id": "8d8bd83a-fcf9-36b1-a627-02562b7154a6",
                                                "text": "He [John Morton] was a learned man, and had a fair library, (rebussed with more in text and tun under it,) partly remaining in the possession of the late earl of Arundel."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fe1102db-cca9-486d-b251-23d60218567d",
                        "source_entry_id": "92570938-f05c-3d43-b565-cce71ebbd163",
                        "source_sense_id": "0777d791-62b9-395f-beab-f90bc14f2cdc",
